WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.100
In membranes from cultured cells, the drug paroxetine fills half of the human

2
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.900
serotonin transporters at only 0.08 nanomolar.

3
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.480
Does that explain why some depressed people improve?

4
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.600
It does not. To see why, look at what the drug acts on.

5
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.200
A transmitter works as a system.

6
00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:28.923
A transmitter system has three parts.

7
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:33.363
The source is the set of neurons that make and release the chemical.

8
00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:35.603
The readers are the receptors.

9
00:00:36.563 --> 00:00:40.243
Some readers are ion channels, which act in about a millisecond.

10
00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:45.643
Others are G-protein-coupled receptors, which act in tens of milliseconds to

11
00:00:45.643 --> 00:00:48.003
seconds through messengers inside the cell.

12
00:00:48.823 --> 00:00:50.623
The off switch ends the signal.

13
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.057
The off switch depends on the transmitter.

14
00:00:54.977 --> 00:01:00.497
Acetylcholine is broken down by an enzyme, acetylcholinesterase, at many synapses.

15
00:01:01.657 --> 00:01:05.057
Glutamate is cleared by transporters in glia and terminals.

16
00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:08.277
No enzyme in the cleft destroys it.

17
00:01:09.077 --> 00:01:10.857
Peptides are cut by peptidases.

18
00:01:11.817 --> 00:01:16.037
The amines, serotonin among them, are carried back into the terminal by

19
00:01:16.037 --> 00:01:20.497
transporters. The serotonin transporter is called SERT.

20
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.030
A drug changes one step.

21
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.910
An agonist activates a reader.

22
00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:32.970
A competitive antagonist takes the reader's own site and prevents activation.

23
00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:39.510
A positive allosteric modulator binds a different site and strengthens the effect.

24
00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.130
An enzyme inhibitor slows the breakdown.

25
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.710
A reuptake blocker occupies the transporter.

26
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:52.230
Paroxetine sits in the central site of SERT, where serotonin binds.

27
00:01:53.183 --> 00:01:56.423
How much of the transporter does the drug fill?

28
00:01:57.163 --> 00:02:03.863
The fraction filled is L over KD plus L, where L is the free drug concentration.

29
00:02:04.803 --> 00:02:10.263
The dissociation constant, KD, is the concentration that fills half the sites.

30
00:02:11.123 --> 00:02:18.083
For paroxetine at human SERT in cell membranes, KD is 0.08 nanomolar.

31
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:22.463
At 0.72 nanomolar, 90% are filled.

32
00:02:23.123 --> 00:02:24.823
The curve flattens at the top.

33
00:02:25.617 --> 00:02:29.017
Filling the transporter is not a clinical effect.

34
00:02:29.877 --> 00:02:32.877
That these drugs block SERT is established.

35
00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:37.337
That depression is caused by low serotonin is a separate claim.

36
00:02:38.317 --> 00:02:42.617
A 2022 umbrella review found no consistent support for it.

37
00:02:43.277 --> 00:02:49.317
A 2018 network meta-analysis found all 21 antidepressants it included more

38
00:02:49.317 --> 00:02:54.137
effective than placebo for acute major depression in adults, with certainty from

39
00:02:54.137 --> 00:02:55.577
moderate to very low.

40
00:02:56.677 --> 00:03:01.877
Both can be true. Aspirin relieves a headache, and headaches are not caused by a

41
00:03:01.877 --> 00:03:06.837
lack of aspirin. A drug's mechanism does not prove what causes the disease.
